  "run_name": "F009-campp-fivefold-fit-capacity-screen",
  "hypothesis": "The historical two-fold protocol leaves only about 662 known encoder-fit files per outer fold because one inner query group is withheld for each known class. A separate five-fold protocol can retain every known class in training while increasing the known fit population to roughly 1326 files per fold. This screen keeps the CAM++ architecture, optimizer recipe, gallery and inner-only rejection policy fixed; only the outer split and available fit population change. It is a new protocol and cannot overwrite or be compared as an exact reproduction of C002b or F005.",
